s","method_description":"The lipophilicity of the compounds 1–5 was determined by using the shake-flask method of octanol/water phase partition. The compounds were dissolved in PBS (pH 7) at concentrations corresponding to absorbance of 0.4 at 488 nm. Octanol (500 μL) was added to a solution of the ruthenium compounds in PBS (500 μL) in 1.5 mL microcentrifuge tubes. The tubes were vigourously shaken for 10 min and the phases were separated by centrifugation at 2000 g for 5 min. The concentration of ruthenium compounds were determined by their absorbance at 488 nm and used to calculate log Poct/w."},{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"Ru-2a","value":-1.24,"value_relation":"=","std":0.38,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","doi":"10.1016/j.jinorgbio.2022.111930","year":2022,"counterion":"O=S(=O)([O-])C(F)(F)F.O=S(=O)([O-])C(F)(F)F","record_id":"MLDB-003370","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The lipophilicity of the complexes was determined experimentally using the “shake flask” method. Nanopure water was used as the aqueous phase and 1-octanol was used as the organic phase. A 100 μM solution of the complex was prepared in 1-octanol and then mixed with and equal volume of water. The solution was shaken vigorously for 5 min and allowed to settle for 24 h while protected from light. The relative concentrations in the water and 1-octanol layers were determined spectrophometrically using a Cary 60 UV–Vis spectrophotometer. LogP was calculated using the absorbance in 1-octanol over the absorbance in water at the lambda max for each compound as follows: Ru-1a 455 nm; Ru-2a 460 nm; Ru-3a 465 nm; Ru-1b 475 nm; Ru-2b 470 nm; Ru-1c 370 nm; Ru-3c 470 nm."}]}